    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1657">

                <pb facs="1311" n="1301" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">119.2/12–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >McConaughy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-28T13:00:00-05:00">December 28,
                            1949—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2490. Fol comments for ur background info only re statements made by Cheng
                    Kang-chi concerning operation radio facilities for official purposes FonServ
                    estab (urtel 5211 Dec 14).</p>
                <pb facs="1312" n="1302" xml:id="pg1302"/>
                <p>Although Brit view use of transmitters by dipl estab as right inherent in dipl
                    usage, US and many other govts do not take this position. Contrary Cheng’s
                    opinion, not customary for Amer dipl and cons offices operate own transmitters.
                    In few cases where they in use permission generally obtained with great
                    difficulty and operations continue at sufferance fon govt. US Communications Act
                        1934<anchor n="68" xml:id="d1657-f1"/> restricts licensing radio
                    transmitters to US cits. Govt does not, therefore, permit ion embs Wash operate
                    radio transmitters any sort. However, no prohibitions re use of receivers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1657-f1" n="68" xml:id="d1657-f1-content">
                <p>Approved June 19, 1934; 48 Stat 1064.</p>
            </note>
